1
00:00:01,930 --> 00:00:03,930
Previously on "Final Space"...

2
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:05,350
At long last, Gary and Avocato

3
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:07,040
rescue Avocato's son,
Little Cato,

4
00:00:07,070 --> 00:00:08,590
from the clutches
of the Lord Commander,

5
00:00:08,620 --> 00:00:10,180
but that dick weed
takes revenge

6
00:00:10,210 --> 00:00:13,390
and teleports a bomb that Avocato finds just in time

7
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:16,560
to sacrifice his life
to save his son.

8
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:20,020
♪♪

9
00:00:20,050 --> 00:00:22,400
I know.
I'll miss him, too.

10
00:00:22,430 --> 00:00:25,370
♪♪

11
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:28,710
H.U.E.: You have three minutes
of oxygen left.

12
00:00:28,750 --> 00:00:31,200
It's cold, H.U.E.

13
00:00:31,230 --> 00:00:32,580
Are you cold?

14
00:00:32,610 --> 00:00:37,380
I only feel two things, Gary -- nothing and nothingness.

15
00:00:37,410 --> 00:00:39,520
You know what?

16
00:00:39,550 --> 00:00:41,380
It's the shade.

17
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:45,390
It's always, like, 10 degrees
colder in the shade.

18
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:48,280
Space is made
entirely of shade.

19
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:49,910
Yeah, I guess it is.

20
00:00:49,940 --> 00:00:52,390
I gotta find some of
that non-shade.

21
00:00:52,430 --> 00:00:54,570
Where the hell is it?

22
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:57,400
Oh, hey.

23
00:00:57,430 --> 00:00:58,880
Oh.[ Beeping ]

24
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:01,750
Oh, boom -- non-shade.

25
00:01:01,780 --> 00:01:05,650
Crap! It's, like, really
freakin' piping hot now.

26
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:14,550
♪♪

27
00:01:14,590 --> 00:01:23,420
♪♪

28
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:32,330
♪♪

29
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:41,440
♪♪

30
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:47,860
♪♪

31
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:49,930
Gary: Avocato?

32
00:01:49,970 --> 00:01:52,940
It's been three days
since you died.

33
00:01:52,970 --> 00:01:54,970
I have to say I'm...

34
00:01:55,010 --> 00:01:57,600
I'm struggling here, man.

35
00:01:57,630 --> 00:02:04,640
♪♪

36
00:02:04,670 --> 00:02:11,640
♪♪

37
00:02:11,680 --> 00:02:18,480
♪♪

38
00:02:18,510 --> 00:02:20,070
You said to
look after your boy,

39
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:23,450
and I can barely
look after myself.

40
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:26,310
I really think you picked
the wrong guy.

41
00:02:26,350 --> 00:02:29,350
Granted, there wasn't a big pool to pick from, but...

42
00:02:29,390 --> 00:02:33,840
I guess what
I'm trying to say is...

43
00:02:33,870 --> 00:02:36,530
I miss you, friend.

44
00:02:36,570 --> 00:02:38,080
What do you think
I should do?

45
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:40,710
I mean, I-I --
I need a sign, man.

46
00:02:40,740 --> 00:02:43,370
You know,
maybe rattle some glasses

47
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:47,510
if I should give him some space
or flicker the lights.

48
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:51,650
You know, just a little flicker
if I should try harder.

49
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:57,210
Any ghost-related stuff at all
would be great.

50
00:03:01,250 --> 00:03:02,830
Or nothing.

51
00:03:02,870 --> 00:03:04,490
Nothing works, too.

52
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:06,220
[ Beeps ]

53
00:03:06,250 --> 00:03:13,330
♪♪

54
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:20,400
♪♪

55
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:23,090
[ Humming ]

56
00:03:26,170 --> 00:03:28,930
What the crap
are you doing?!

57
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:30,690
KVN is making
helpful repairs.

58
00:03:30,720 --> 00:03:32,280
There! Boomtown!
No more hole.

59
00:03:32,310 --> 00:03:35,210
Hole?! That was the door
to the bathroom!

60
00:03:38,110 --> 00:03:40,910
Oh! I thought it was
a huge rectangular hole.

61
00:03:40,940 --> 00:03:42,390
Ugh!
How?!

62
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:45,390
That huge rectangular hole was
the door to the bathroom!

63
00:03:45,430 --> 00:03:48,220
You sure?
Yes!
Yes, I'm -- Yes!

64
00:03:48,260 --> 00:03:51,300
[ Chuckles ] Well, that puts
you in a situation, huh?

65
00:03:51,330 --> 00:03:52,880
H.U.E.: Gary?
Yeah?

66
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:54,920
I have news for you.What is it, H.U.E.?

67
00:03:54,950 --> 00:03:59,160
Three, two, one...

68
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:02,410
Gary, your prison sentence
aboard the Galaxy 1

69
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:03,650
is now complete.

70
00:04:03,690 --> 00:04:04,930
That's gre--
Wait, say what?

71
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:06,590
You're free, Gary.

72
00:04:06,620 --> 00:04:07,830
Free?

73
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:09,170
This isn't a joke?

74
00:04:09,210 --> 00:04:10,590
I mean,
I-I'm really free?

75
00:04:10,620 --> 00:04:14,560
Yes, Gary. What are you
going to do now?

76
00:04:14,590 --> 00:04:16,290
[ Munching ]

77
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:18,810
Yes!
Oh, I'm free!

78
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:20,740
All these long years,

79
00:04:20,770 --> 00:04:23,470
and these freedom cookies
are mine!

80
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:24,980
[ Munching ]

81
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:27,990
[ Clang! ]

82
00:04:29,540 --> 00:04:32,470
Gary? You should talk
to Little Cato.

83
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:35,200
[ Grunting ]

84
00:04:37,380 --> 00:04:38,790
[ Grunts ]

85
00:04:38,830 --> 00:04:41,860
[ Panting ]

86
00:04:41,900 --> 00:04:44,450
[ Grunting ]

87
00:04:44,490 --> 00:04:46,870
"I think you need
to talk to Little Cato.

88
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:48,700
I think you need to,
uh, crawl in a vent

89
00:04:48,730 --> 00:04:50,490
and talk to Little Cato."

90
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:56,360
[ Screams ]

91
00:04:57,880 --> 00:04:59,160
[ Wheezes ]

92
00:04:59,190 --> 00:05:01,330
Hey, where'd you get
all those cookies?

93
00:05:01,370 --> 00:05:02,810
You want them?
They suck.

94
00:05:02,850 --> 00:05:04,540
They do.
They do suck.

95
00:05:04,580 --> 00:05:07,470
Five years for these little
round pieces of suckage!

96
00:05:07,510 --> 00:05:10,340
Get to the point.
I'm a busy guy.

97
00:05:10,370 --> 00:05:12,690
Well, hmm.

98
00:05:12,720 --> 00:05:13,830
All right, buddy,

99
00:05:13,860 --> 00:05:15,660
what can I do
to make you happy?

100
00:05:15,690 --> 00:05:17,480
Name anything.
Anything?

101
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:19,490
Freakin' anything.
Anything?

102
00:05:19,520 --> 00:05:21,660
I just said freakin' anything.
Anything.

103
00:05:21,700 --> 00:05:25,490
Can you get me to
the Lord Commander?

104
00:05:25,530 --> 00:05:27,080
Okay.
Possibly.

105
00:05:27,110 --> 00:05:28,320
What do you want to do?

106
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:30,390
I want to
slit his throat

107
00:05:30,430 --> 00:05:34,090
and splash
in his life juice.

108
00:05:35,230 --> 00:05:36,750
Oh. Good Lord,
that's dark.

109
00:05:36,780 --> 00:05:38,020
Okay, well...

110
00:05:38,060 --> 00:05:40,020
[ Chuckles ]
Sounds like a fantastic idea.

111
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:41,410
Count me in!

112
00:05:41,440 --> 00:05:43,410
[ Laughs ] I never thought
I'd be creating

113
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:47,410
a murder squad with
a small boy, but here we are.

114
00:05:48,580 --> 00:05:50,520
Is this...

115
00:05:50,550 --> 00:05:51,760
Is this my father's room?

116
00:05:51,790 --> 00:05:53,280
Hell yeah, it is.

117
00:05:55,970 --> 00:05:57,490
Oh, my gosh,
look at all the crap.

118
00:05:57,520 --> 00:05:59,700
All right, well, Avocato's
gotta have big boom sticks

119
00:05:59,730 --> 00:06:01,110
in here somewhere.

120
00:06:01,150 --> 00:06:02,940
What did
you think of him?
Your dad?

121
00:06:02,980 --> 00:06:05,390
Well, he was a short-tempered,
angry grouch.

122
00:06:05,430 --> 00:06:07,530
[ Chuckles ]
I loved that about him.

123
00:06:07,570 --> 00:06:09,880
Me, too.
Plus, he cared about you.

124
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:11,950
Man, I mean,
more than anything.

125
00:06:11,990 --> 00:06:13,300
You think so?
I know so.

126
00:06:13,330 --> 00:06:14,540
He would never
shut up about you.

127
00:06:14,580 --> 00:06:16,030
I mean, every day,
"Little Cato --

128
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:17,750
we gotta save Little Cato.
He's injured.

129
00:06:17,790 --> 00:06:19,930
He's my boy.
Let's find him."

130
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:21,890
You know, I do not jest,
the man loved you.

131
00:06:21,930 --> 00:06:23,450
He never said that to me.

132
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:26,210
He said it when
he gave his life to save you.

133
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:28,940
That was love
in action mode --

134
00:06:28,970 --> 00:06:30,420
Avocato style.

135
00:06:30,450 --> 00:06:35,630
♪♪

136
00:06:35,670 --> 00:06:40,810
♪♪

137
00:06:40,840 --> 00:06:43,090
[ Rumbling ]

138
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:45,920
Heck chicklets!
We got it!

139
00:06:45,950 --> 00:06:47,540
Here you go!
You ready?

140
00:06:47,570 --> 00:06:50,230
Let's tear the Lord Commander
a new butthole.

141
00:06:50,270 --> 00:06:52,170
Yes!
Maybe even three!

142
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:53,890
Or four.
Four of them?

143
00:06:53,930 --> 00:06:56,830
10. 10 painfully
wide-open buttholes!

144
00:06:56,860 --> 00:06:59,240
We're gonna cover him
in buttholes.

145
00:06:59,280 --> 00:07:02,620
That's a -- that's, like, 50
to 55 buttholes right there!

146
00:07:02,660 --> 00:07:04,800
KVN wants to cover him
in buttholes, too!

147
00:07:04,830 --> 00:07:06,250
We're coming,
deal with it!

148
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:08,350
All right, fine.
We shall be called

149
00:07:08,390 --> 00:07:09,770
the Legion of Murdering

150
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:12,980
an Irritatingly
Power-thirsty Pint-sized Imp

151
00:07:13,010 --> 00:07:18,120
into a Plethora
of Butthoooooles!

152
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:25,060
♪♪

153
00:07:27,550 --> 00:07:32,170
H.U.E.: Quinn, only 48 hours till the breach consumes Earth.

154
00:07:32,210 --> 00:07:33,520
Until we fix the ship,

155
00:07:33,550 --> 00:07:36,140
we cannot engage
our lightfold engines,

156
00:07:36,170 --> 00:07:39,280
and you have
a more immediate problem.

157
00:07:39,320 --> 00:07:41,530
H.U.E.,
what is he doing?

158
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:43,460
I can only hypothesize,

159
00:07:43,490 --> 00:07:45,600
but I think they are
going to pick a fight.

160
00:07:45,630 --> 00:07:47,010
That idiot!

161
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:53,020
Gary, we don't
have time for this!

162
00:07:53,050 --> 00:07:54,680
We've got bigger problems!

163
00:07:54,710 --> 00:07:56,230
Oh, right.
Tunes!

164
00:07:56,260 --> 00:07:57,780
[ Chuckles ]
Thanks, Quinn.

165
00:07:57,820 --> 00:07:59,230
H.U.E.,
play the good stuff.

166
00:07:59,270 --> 00:08:02,650
I'm talking about war trumpets,
rain sticks,

167
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:04,510
soul-crushing crumhorns

168
00:08:04,550 --> 00:08:07,900
to stir the hearts
of these merry men.

169
00:08:07,930 --> 00:08:09,410
And piccolos and clarinets.

170
00:08:09,450 --> 00:08:11,140
No piccolos or clarinets!

171
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:13,900
Right.
Angelic violins.No!

172
00:08:13,940 --> 00:08:15,800
[ Soft music plays ]

173
00:08:15,840 --> 00:08:17,320
Oh, H.U.E., what is this?

174
00:08:17,350 --> 00:08:19,560
The good stuff, Gary.That is not the good stuff!

175
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:22,390
Where are the war trumpets,
the rain sticks?

176
00:08:22,430 --> 00:08:23,570
This is so sad, Gary.

177
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:26,090
It makes me think about
all the people I've loved

178
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:27,640
who have died, like --

179
00:08:27,670 --> 00:08:28,880
Don't -- Don't say it.

180
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:31,920
Avocato.
Oh!
[ Sobbing ]

181
00:08:31,950 --> 00:08:35,920
My bro is dead!

182
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:38,750
Can you take all of that
over there?

183
00:08:38,790 --> 00:08:40,410
Maybe I should.

184
00:08:40,450 --> 00:08:41,900
Sorry, small fry.

185
00:08:41,930 --> 00:08:44,450
I didn't foresee
my emotional shielding

186
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:47,210
getting shut down
so quickly!

187
00:08:47,250 --> 00:08:49,870
[ Sobbing ]
Chookity!

188
00:08:49,900 --> 00:08:52,080
Shut the hell up,
Mooncake!

189
00:08:52,110 --> 00:08:55,530
[ Sobbing ]
Oh, I'm so sad!

190
00:08:55,560 --> 00:08:57,530
♪♪

191
00:08:57,570 --> 00:08:58,710
Little Cato,

192
00:08:58,740 --> 00:09:01,020
I am not detecting
the Lord Commander

193
00:09:01,050 --> 00:09:02,680
on that heavy incinerator.

194
00:09:02,710 --> 00:09:04,190
I don't care.

195
00:09:04,230 --> 00:09:06,400
This is for my dad!

196
00:09:09,510 --> 00:09:12,580
In hindsight, this wasn't
the greatest idea.

197
00:09:13,820 --> 00:09:14,790
[ Screams ]

198
00:09:14,830 --> 00:09:16,030
Quinn: What was that?!

199
00:09:16,070 --> 00:09:19,070
Gary, are you okay?
Gary? Gary?!

200
00:09:19,110 --> 00:09:21,280
Gary!
[ Screaming ]

201
00:09:21,310 --> 00:09:31,080
♪♪

202
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:34,050
Oh, my audio processing unit.
I can't hear you.

203
00:09:34,090 --> 00:09:35,430
What, what?

204
00:09:35,470 --> 00:09:37,430
What, what?

205
00:09:37,470 --> 00:09:39,570
[ Engine rumbles ]

206
00:09:39,610 --> 00:09:43,890
♪♪

207
00:09:43,920 --> 00:09:45,370
[ Tone chimes ]

208
00:09:48,860 --> 00:09:50,590
[ Tone chimes ]

209
00:09:50,620 --> 00:09:56,180
♪♪

210
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:11,850
[ Grunts ]

211
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:14,130
Small fry?
Hey, wake up.

212
00:10:17,130 --> 00:10:19,580
[ Buzzes ]
Did you say something?

213
00:10:21,820 --> 00:10:23,310
[ Monitor beeping ]

214
00:10:23,340 --> 00:10:27,210
Avocato picked the worst guy
to watch over his son.

215
00:10:27,240 --> 00:10:31,110
I am a bad-luck magnet.[ Humming ]

216
00:10:31,140 --> 00:10:32,450
Is he breathing?

217
00:10:32,490 --> 00:10:36,530
Great news, guys.
Little Cato is breathing.

218
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:41,880
You saved my life.

219
00:10:41,910 --> 00:10:43,430
Who are you?

220
00:10:45,610 --> 00:10:47,120
Hi, Gary.

221
00:10:47,160 --> 00:10:48,500
Quinn?!
Gary, I--

222
00:10:48,540 --> 00:10:49,400
[ Screams ]

223
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:52,340
What the
tough titty wompas?

224
00:10:56,410 --> 00:10:57,690
Who are you?

225
00:10:57,720 --> 00:10:59,030
Wha?
I'm you.

226
00:10:59,070 --> 00:11:00,310
But you can't be me.

227
00:11:00,340 --> 00:11:02,970
I know that
because I'm already me.

228
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:05,140
What?No, I'm really you,

229
00:11:05,180 --> 00:11:07,040
just from the future.

230
00:11:07,080 --> 00:11:08,520
Hey, future Quinn,
I'm KVN,

231
00:11:08,560 --> 00:11:11,420
Gary's deep-space insanity
avoidance companion.

232
00:11:11,460 --> 00:11:14,320
[ Chuckles ] We're just
the bestest of friends.

233
00:11:14,360 --> 00:11:16,360
Shut up, KVN.Good Lord, that's hot.

234
00:11:16,390 --> 00:11:18,910
But the two of us together,
isn't that a paradox?

235
00:11:18,950 --> 00:11:20,190
Shouldn't the universe
explode?

236
00:11:20,230 --> 00:11:21,230
Excellent question.

237
00:11:21,260 --> 00:11:22,540
Apparently not.

238
00:11:22,570 --> 00:11:23,890
Excellent answer.

239
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:25,440
But...why?

240
00:11:25,470 --> 00:11:28,270
'Cause Einstein's a jerk.
How am I supposed to know?

241
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:31,930
If it helps, you can call me
by my code name --

242
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:33,620
Nightfall.
Nightfall?

243
00:11:33,650 --> 00:11:35,280
That's super lame.

244
00:11:35,310 --> 00:11:36,620
Did I come up with that?

245
00:11:36,660 --> 00:11:37,760
No.
He did.

246
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:39,110
[ Laughs ]

247
00:11:39,140 --> 00:11:41,730
Quinns, Quinns, stop fighting
with yourselves.

248
00:11:41,770 --> 00:11:45,220
Gotta say, Gary,
I missed your wit.

249
00:11:45,250 --> 00:11:48,290
Wit?! He took Little Cato
on a stupid suicide mission!

250
00:11:48,320 --> 00:11:49,950
What's wrong with you?!

251
00:11:49,980 --> 00:11:52,020
You're a danger
to all of us.

252
00:11:52,050 --> 00:11:53,740
♪♪

253
00:11:53,780 --> 00:11:56,190
Don't disagree.
My best friend's dead.

254
00:11:56,230 --> 00:11:58,130
I almost got his son killed.

255
00:11:58,160 --> 00:11:59,890
Now that my
prison sentence is up,

256
00:11:59,920 --> 00:12:02,650
maybe it's a good time for me
and Mooncake to move on.

257
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:05,240
A great time.

258
00:12:05,270 --> 00:12:07,860
All right then.
Peace out.

259
00:12:07,890 --> 00:12:09,450
Just gonna get my keys.

260
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:11,280
Where the crap are my keys?

261
00:12:11,310 --> 00:12:14,280
Oh, oh, oh.
That's a few coins.

262
00:12:14,310 --> 00:12:16,210
Oh, yeah.
I-I don't have keys.

263
00:12:16,250 --> 00:12:17,970
Okay, well...

264
00:12:18,010 --> 00:12:19,630
Peace out again.

265
00:12:22,670 --> 00:12:24,320
Quinn, Gary can't leave.

266
